  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Cut the <b>eggplants</b> into <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 cm</span> dice, toss with the <b>salt</b> and leave 10 minutes. Squeeze them hard.</li><li>Fry in the <b>oil</b> over medium heat until soft, 4 minutes. Add the <b>soy</b>, <b>sugar</b> and <b>sake</b> and cook, stirring, until the liquid is gone and the eggplant is dark and glossy, about <b>6 minutes</b>.</li><li>Nigihaya mixes its eggplant all through the rice instead of hiding it in the middle. Do the same: fold it into warm rice, then shape.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
