  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Shape as on the <a href=\"onigiri.html\">onigiri page</a>, but bigger and looser: about <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"120\" data-s=\"0\">120 g</span></b> of rice, packed only enough to hold.</li><li>Put a heaped tablespoon of filling in the well, close the rice over it, then set a little more <b>on top</b>, so you can see what's inside. That's how Bongo and Togoshi-ya show theirs.</li><li>Wrap a strip of <b>nori</b> around the base and up the sides, leaving the top with the filling open. Eat within the hour, while the nori is crisp.</li><li>Good doubles: soboro with a cured yolk, mentai mayo on takana.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
